h3. Problem
{{RoundRobinPartitioner}} creates its per-topic counter with {{new AtomicInteger(0)}} (trunk: RoundRobinPartitioner.java, {{nextValue}}). Every producer instance therefore starts from the first entry of {{availablePartitionsForTopic}}, and all producers in the same cluster see the same partition list.

When several producers start at the same time (e.g. a Kubernetes rollout) and each sends the same number of records, their counters stay equal. The k-th record of every producer goes to the same partition. Instead of spreading load, N producers stack N records on the same few partitions.

Round robin is only guaranteed within one producer, so this is not a correctness bug. However, it makes the multi-producer result worse than the default sticky partitioner, which picks a random partition ({{ThreadLocalRandom}}).

h3. Reproduction (kafka-clients 3.9.2 and 4.2.1)
{code:java}
Node node = new Node(0, "localhost", 9092);
List<PartitionInfo> infos = new ArrayList<>();
for (int p = 0; p < 100; p++)
    infos.add(new PartitionInfo("t", p, node, new Node[]{node}, new Node[]{node}));
Cluster cluster = new Cluster("c", List.of(node), infos, Set.of(), Set.of());

// 10 producers (one partitioner each) started together, 5 records each
Map<Integer, Integer> perPartition = new TreeMap<>();
for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
    RoundRobinPartitioner rr = new RoundRobinPartitioner();
    for (int k = 0; k < 5; k++)
        perPartition.merge(rr.partition("t", null, null, null, null, cluster), 1, Integer::sum);
}
System.out.println(perPartition);
// 3.9.2 and 4.2.1: {0=10, 1=10, 2=10, 3=10, 4=10}  -> 50 records on 5 of 100 partitions
{code}

h3. Observed in production
* 27 consumer pods each re-publish records to a 216-partition topic with {{partitioner.class=RoundRobinPartitioner}}.
* An upstream round-robin step delivers the same number of records to every pod, so the counters never drift apart.
* Over 4 hours after a rollout, 2,142 records landed on only 82 of 216 partitions, 77 of them with exactly 27 records (= number of pods). 134 partitions received nothing.
* Partition skew (max / average inflow) rose from 7.9 with the default sticky partitioner to 14.4 after switching to RoundRobinPartitioner.

h3. Proposed change
Start each counter at a random value, as the pre-2.4 {{DefaultPartitioner}} did ({{new AtomicInteger(ThreadLocalRandom.current().nextInt())}}):
{code:java}
AtomicInteger counter = topicCounterMap.computeIfAbsent(topic,
        k -> new AtomicInteger(ThreadLocalRandom.current().nextInt()));
{code}
* No need to know the partition count up front: {{partition()}} already applies {{Utils.toPositive(next) % availablePartitions.size()}} on every call.
* Round robin within one producer is unchanged. Only the starting partition becomes random.
* In a replay of the same production traffic (27 producers, 216 partitions), the busiest partition of each burst receives on average 2.2x its even share instead of 15.8x (1.0x = perfectly even).

