h3. Problem

When a tiered-storage broker restarts with existing cached indexes exceeding remote.log.index.file.cache.total.size.bytes (for example, after reducing that setting), RemoteIndexCache can leave evicted index files on disk until the next restart.

The constructor [calls init() before cleanerScheduler.startup()|https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/c3cbf35565aaf8754f266320f8f8a73a7189abd2/storage/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/storage/internals/log/RemoteIndexCache.java#L151-L158]. Restoring entries can trigger Caffeine eviction. The eviction listener [renames index files to .deleted and schedules cleanup|https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/c3cbf35565aaf8754f266320f8f8a73a7189abd2/storage/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/storage/internals/log/RemoteIndexCache.java#L248-L259], but [KafkaScheduler ignores tasks submitted before startup|https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/c3cbf35565aaf8754f266320f8f8a73a7189abd2/server-common/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/server/util/KafkaScheduler.java#L144-L165]. Starting the scheduler later does not replay those tasks.

