{{Utils.atomicMoveWithFallback}} fsyncs the parent directory of {{target}} in a {{finally}} block. If the move fails and the fsync fails too, the fsync exception replaces the move exception with nothing suppressed. Which file failed to move, and why, is lost.

{code:java}
// clients/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/common/utils/Utils.java (logging elided)
try {
    Files.move(source, target, ATOMIC_MOVE);
} catch (IOException outer) {
    try {
        Files.move(source, target, REPLACE_EXISTING);
    } catch (IOException inner) {
        inner.addSuppressed(outer);
        throw inner;                       // discarded if flushDir below throws
    }
} finally {
    if (needFlushParentDir) {
        flushDir(target.toAbsolutePath().normalize().getParent());
    }
}
{code}

